//? Title: Winnow: A Sparse Rule Among Correlated Pixels
//? Subtitle: Multiplicative updates, a potential-function mistake bound and the limits of observed accuracy
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Winnow learns Boolean threshold rules by multiplying active weights on
mistakes. We use the 8 by 8 measurements in `dm::datasets::digits()` to
construct a known two-pixel OR target, then hide those two attributes among
other thresholded pixels. This is a sparse-concept experiment, not digit
recognition. We derive a logarithmic mistake bound using target-weight
promotions and a total-weight potential, inspect the actual shared training
loop's trace, and evaluate a frozen rule on held-out images. Counterfactual
Boolean probes show why perfect accuracy on observed images need not mean
the learned rule equals the target on every Boolean vector.
)

\toc

> The data and the constructed target

The dataset contains 1797 handwritten images with 64 integer intensities
from 0 to 16 and a numeric digit label. Pixel indices are row-major on the
8 by 8 grid. We deliberately ignore the original digit response. Set a
Boolean attribute to one when its intensity strictly exceeds eight, and
define the target as the OR of `pixel_27` and `pixel_28`. These adjacent
central pixels are useful for a reproducible sparse-rule demonstration.
Neither the cutoff nor the target is estimated from training outcomes.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/winnow_pixels.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  const auto digits = dm::datasets::digits();
  std::print("{}\n",digits.select({"pixel_27","pixel_28","digit"}).head(8).to_md());
  const auto binary = dm::algorithms::winnow_disjunction_data(digits,{"pixel_27","pixel_28"},{"pixel_27","pixel_28"});
  std::print("\n{}\n",(binary | dm::group_by("target") | dm::summarise(dm::agg::n("images"))).to_md());
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  dm::graphics::RPlot::create().points(digits.get_column("pixel_27").values(),digits.get_column("pixel_28").values(),
      "images",dm::RGB{37,99,235},3)
      .abline_v(8,dm::RGB{220,38,38},1).abline_h(8,dm::RGB{220,38,38},1)
      .title("Two observed pixel intensities define a Boolean OR target")
      .x_label("pixel 27 intensity").y_label("pixel 28 intensity")
      .size(900,540).save_svg("build/winnow_pixels.svg");
}
```
