\image(figures/winnow_passes.svg)
// result_end
\caption(The first pass makes 15 online updates, although its final weights already classify every training image correctly. The next pass makes none. Test rows are evaluated without any weight update.)
\alttext(A two-pass chart showing online mistakes falling from fifteen to zero while the cumulative update count stays at fifteen.)

There are nine promotions and six demotions, below the derived bound
\(2+6\log_2(128)=44\). The frozen rule also makes no mistakes on the
539 held-out images. Since the engineered target is mostly positive,
ordinary accuracy should be read with its false-positive and false-negative
counts rather than alone. These results concern a known pixel rule, not
the ten handwritten-digit classes.

> Final weights and counterexamples outside the observed image support

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/winnow_weights.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  const auto digits = dm::datasets::digits(); auto predictors = digits.columns();
  predictors.erase(std::remove(predictors.begin(),predictors.end(),"digit"),predictors.end());
  const auto [train,test] = dm::stats::train_test_split(digits,0.3,42);
  const auto fit = dm::algorithms::winnow_fit(dm::algorithms::winnow_disjunction_data(train,predictors,{"pixel_27","pixel_28"}));
  std::print("{}\n",(fit.weights | dm::arrange(dm::desc("weight"))).head(12).to_md());
  std::print("\n{}\n",dm::algorithms::winnow_disjunction_probes(fit,{"pixel_27","pixel_28"}).to_md(6));
  const auto relevant = fit.weights.filter([](const auto& r) {
    return r.get_string("feature")=="pixel_27" || r.get_string("feature")=="pixel_28";
  });
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  dm::graphics::RPlot::create().points(fit.weights.get_column("index").values(),fit.weights.get_column("log2_weight").values(),
      "all weights",dm::RGB{37,99,235},3)
      .points(relevant.get_column("index").values(),relevant.get_column("log2_weight").values(),"target weights",dm::RGB{220,38,38},6)
      .abline_h(std::log2(fit.model.threshold),dm::RGB{100,100,100},1)
      .title("The target pixels dominate, but a threshold tie still predicts zero")
      .x_label("row-major pixel index").y_label("log2(weight)").size(1000,500).save_svg("build/winnow_weights.svg");
}
```
